		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>voici ce que je teste en local mais y a rien sur les fichiers sauvegarder 0Ko</p><p>DST=/D/backup/dump<br />login=postgres<br />password=postgres<br />host=localhost<br />db=postgres</p><br /><p>&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; if [ $db = postgres ]; then<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; mkdir -p $DST/$host/$db<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; datetime=$(date +%Y_%m_%d-%H_%M_%S)<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; pg_dump --host=$host --username=$login --password=$password $db | gzip -c &gt; $DST/$host/$db/$db&quot;-&quot;$datetime.sql.gz<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; </p><p>&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; fi</p><p>exit 0</p>]]></content>
